      "content": "If you hear a hissing sound or see smoke from your phone, immediately power off the device, place it in a non-conductive container (like a bag of rice or an antistatic bag) to cut off the current, and evacuate the area to avoid smoke inhalation and potential fire hazard. Do not attempt to handle the phone. Call your phone carrier's emergency services or the manufacturer's helpline for further guidance. Leave the phone alone, avoiding any contact to prevent personal injury or exacerbation of the hazard. Contact professional battery and electronic waste disposal services to collect the phone. Report the incident to the proper local authorities if necessary, as there may be additional safety protocols or investigations involved. Disposing of or handling such situations should always be done with a focus on safety and preventing potentially dangerous situations.",
